===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|fruyt}}, {{m|enm|frut|t=fruits and vegetables}}, from {{der|en|fro|fruit|t=produce, fruits and vegetables}}, from {{der|en|la|frūctus|t=enjoyment, proceeds, profits, produce, income}} and {{m|la|frūx|t=crop, produce, fruit}} (compare {{cog|la|fruor|t=have the benefit of, to use, to enjoy}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰruHg-||to make use of, to have enjoyment of}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|brook|t=to bear, tolerate}} and {{cog|de|brauchen|t=to need}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|wæstm}}.

