===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}} (''see [[#Usage notes|Usage notes]] for discussion of plural'')

# {{senseid|en|botany}}{{lb|en|botany}} A product of fertilization in a plant, specifically:
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1640|location=London|author=John Parkinson| title=Theatrum botanicum: the Theater of Plants; or, An Herball of a Large Extent| page=1063| pageurl=https://hdl.handle.net/2027/ucm.5326186323?urlappend=%3Bseq=195| text=[A]fter the flower is past commeth the '''fruit''' in long pods, every seede bunching out like the pods of Orobus and as bigge almost as the smaller Pease.}}
## The [[seed]]-bearing part of a plant; often [[edible]], colourful, fragrant, and sweet or sour; produced from a floral [[ovary]] after fertilization.
## The spores of {{l|en|cryptogams}} and their accessory organs.
# Any sweet or sour, edible part of a plant that resembles seed-bearing fruit {{q|see former sense}} even if it does not develop from a floral ovary.
## A sweet or sweetish [[vegetable]], such as the [[petiole]]s of [[rhubarb]], that resembles a true fruit or is used in cookery as if it was a fruit.
# An [[end result]], [[effect]]{{,}} or [[consequence]]; [[advantageous]] or [[disadvantageous]] [[result]].
#: {{ux|en|His long nights in the office eventually bore '''fruit''' when his business boomed and he was given a raise.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3|II|i|passage=the '''fruit''' of rashness}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Isaiah|3|10|passage=They shall eat the '''fruit''' of their doings.}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|chapter=20|passage=The '''fruits''' of this education became visible.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2019-07-11|author=John Thornhill| title=Does tech threaten to rerun the worst of the Industrial Revolution?| journal=w:Financial Times| url=https://www.ft.com/content/f1b84f22-a25b-11e9-974c-ad1c6ab5efd1| passage=It is incontestably the case that future generations enjoyed the extraordinary '''fruits''' of the Industrial Revolution’s “great enrichment”.}}
# {{lb|en|attributive}} Of, belonging to, related to, or having fruit or its characteristics; {{q|of living things}} producing or consuming fruit.
#: {{ux|en|fresh-squeezed '''fruit''' juice}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''fruit''' salad}}
#: {{ux|en|an artificial '''fruit''' flavor}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''fruit''' tree}}
# {{lb|en|dated|colloquial|derogatory}} A [[homosexual]] [[man]]; {{lb|en|derogatory|figurative}} an [[effeminate]] [[man]]. {{defdate|from 1900}}<!--See talk page-->
#* {{RQ:William Burroughs Junkie|year=1977|page=66|passage="Moishe just checked in," he said. "He's a panhandler ''and'' a '''fruit'''. A disgrace to the Jewish race."}}
#* {{quote-av|en|role=Ian Faith|actor=Tony Hendra|year=1984|title=This is Spinal Tap| passage=I'm not talking to this twisted '''fruit''' anymore!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title={{w|Ghost World (comics)|Ghost World}}|isbn=0-224-06088-0|chapter=Garage Sale|publisher=Jonathan Cape| year_published=2000| year=1997| author=w:Daniel Clowes| page=15| passage=Aww, but he's so cute! / He's a '''fruit'''… Oh my fucking god! You will not believe who was here today!}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[offspring|Offspring]] from a sexual union.
#: {{ux|en|The litter was the '''fruit''' of the union between our whippet and their terrier.}}
